{{also|Muffin}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|en|moofin}}, of uncertain origin. Possibly from {{bor|en|nds|muffen}}, plural of {{m|nds|muffe|t=small cake}}, or perhaps a diminutive of {{m|nds|muffe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmʌfɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-muffin.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌfɪn}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|British}} A type of [[flattish]] bun, usually cut in two [[horizontally]], [[toast]]ed and spread with butter, etc, before being eaten.
# {{lb|en|US}} A type of individual bread such as corn, bran, banana or zucchini bread often sliced and spread with butter, etc before being eaten.
# {{lb|en|especially US}} (informally) A [[cupcake]] without frosting, but sometimes glazed.
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[mechanism]] used in the [[w:Java Network Launching Protocol|Java Network Launching Protocol]] [[analogous]] to the [[cookie]] mechanism and which permits a program running in a [[browser]] to perform operations on a client machine.
# {{lb|en|slang}} {{non-gloss definition|Term of endearment.}}<!--, e.g. "nuffin' muffin"-->
#: ''I love you, '''muffin'''!''
# {{lb|en|sexual slang}} A [[vulva]].
# {{lb|en|baseball|slang}} A less [[talented]] player; one who [[muff]]s, or drops the ball.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A charming, attractive young man. <!--Ch1908: "one who dangles after a young woman"--> {{rfex|en}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[small]] [[plate]], smaller than a [[twiffler]]. <!--Chambers 1908-->

====Quotations====
{{sense|computing term}}
* '''2001''': The name/value pairs provided by the PersistenceService are similar to browser cookies. The Java Web Start implementation honors this legacy by naming the pairs "'''muffins'''." &mdash; ''JNLP and Java Web Start'', Sun Developer Network, Technical Articles and Tips, 30 May 2001.
{{sense|the vulva}}
* '''1989''': I wanna be stuffin’ Martha’s '''muffin'''!!!, &mdash; Mojo Nixon and Skid Roper ''Stuffin’ Martha’s Muffin''.

